+++ b/libdiscover/backends/Dnf5Backend/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,221 @@
+# DNF 5 Backend for KDE Discover
+
+A native backend for KDE Discover that uses **libdnf5** to manage RPM packages
+directly, bypassing PackageKit.  It is intended for Fedora 41+ and other
+distributions that ship DNF 5 as their primary package manager.
+
+## Overview
+
+The backend provides:
+
+| Class               | Purpose                                         |
+|---------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
+| `Dnf5Backend`       | Plugin entry-point; initialises libdnf5, loads  |
+|                     | repo metadata and populates the resource list.  |
+| `Dnf5Resource`      | Wraps a `libdnf5::rpm::Package` with the        |
+|                     | `AbstractResource` interface Discover expects.  |
+| `Dnf5Transaction`   | Executes install / remove operations through    |
+|                     | `libdnf5::Goal` and `libdnf5::base::Transaction`. |
+| `Dnf5SourcesBackend`| Exposes enabled/disabled repositories in the    |
+|                     | Discover "Sources" view.                        |
+
+The plugin is compiled as `dnf5-backend.so` and installed into the
+`discover` Qt plugin directory so Discover picks it up automatically.
+
+### Architecture notes
+
+* **Exception handling** — libdnf5 reports errors via C++ exceptions.  KDE
+  builds normally compile with `-fno-exceptions`, so the backend CMakeLists
+  adds `-fexceptions` for this target only.  All libdnf5 calls are wrapped
+  in `try / catch`.
+
+* **Non-copyable Base** — `libdnf5::Base` cannot be copied or moved, so the
+  backend stores it as `std::unique_ptr<libdnf5::Base>`.  When repo metadata
+  needs a full refresh (e.g. `checkForUpdates()`), the old Base is replaced
+  with a new one.
+
+* **Synchronous loading** — Repo metadata is loaded synchronously in the
+  constructor.  On a typical Fedora system this takes 1–3 seconds, which is
+  acceptable for the initial load.
+
+## Build requirements
+
+* **libdnf5 ≥ 5.0** (plus its transitive dependencies: libsolv, librepo,
+  librpm, libgpgme, libmodulemd, json-c, toml-c, libcurl, sdbus-c++)
+* **Qt 6.9+**, **KF6 6.17+**, and **Extra CMake Modules (ECM)**
+* **pkg-config** (used to locate libdnf5)
+
+### Installing libdnf5 from source (if not packaged)
+
+```bash
+# Install build dependencies (Debian/Ubuntu — adapt for your distro)
+sudo apt install libsolv-dev librepo-dev librpm-dev libgpgme-dev \
+     libmodulemd-dev libjson-c-dev libtoml-c-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev \
+     libsdbus-c++-dev
+
+cd /path/to/dnf5-source
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake .. \
+  -DWITH_PERL5=OFF -DWITH_PYTHON3=OFF -DWITH_RUBY=OFF \
+  -DWITH_MAN=OFF  -DWITH_HTML=OFF    -DWITH_TESTS=OFF \
+  -DWITH_GO=OFF   -DWITH_PLUGIN_RHSM=OFF
+make -j$(nproc) libdnf5
+sudo make install
+sudo ldconfig
+```
+
+On Fedora you can simply `sudo dnf install libdnf5-devel`.
+
+## Building the backend
+
+The backend integrates into the normal Discover build.  If libdnf5 is
+detected, it is enabled automatically.
+
+```bash
+cd /path/to/discover
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr
+make -j$(nproc)
+```
+
+To build **only** the backend and its CLI test tools:
+
+```bash
+cmake --build . --target dnf5-backend dnf5_cli_list dnf5_cli_info dnf5_cli_updates
+```
+
+The CMake option `BUILD_Dnf5Backend` (default `ON`) can be set to `OFF` to
+skip the backend even when libdnf5 is available:
+
+```bash
+cmake .. -DBUILD_Dnf5Backend=OFF
+```
+
+## CLI test tools
+
+Three command-line tools are built under
+`libdiscover/backends/Dnf5Backend/tests/`.  They load the `dnf5-backend`
+plugin through Discover's own `ResourcesModel`, so every code path exercised
+by the GUI is also reachable from the terminal.
+
+### Running the tools
+
+From the build directory, set `QT_PLUGIN_PATH` so that the plugin can be
+found:
+
+```bash
+export QT_PLUGIN_PATH=$PWD/bin
+```
+
+#### `dnf5_cli_list` — list and search packages
+
+```
+Usage: dnf5_cli_list [options]
+
+Options:
+  --search <term>   Search packages by name or summary
+  --installed        Show installed packages only
+  --upgradeable      Show upgradeable packages only
+  -h, --help         Show help
+```
+
+Examples:
+
+```bash
+# List all known packages
+./bin/dnf5_cli_list
+
+# Search for "kernel"
+./bin/dnf5_cli_list --search kernel
+
+# List only installed packages
+./bin/dnf5_cli_list --installed
+
+# List only upgradeable packages
+./bin/dnf5_cli_list --upgradeable
+```
+
+#### `dnf5_cli_info` — show detailed package information
+
+```
+Usage: dnf5_cli_info [options] <package-name>
+
+Arguments:
+  package   Package name to look up
+
+Options:
+  -h, --help   Show help
+```
+
+Example:
+
+```bash
+./bin/dnf5_cli_info bash
+```
+
+Output includes: name, summary, state (installed / available / upgradeable),
+installed version, available version, size, section (RPM group), origin
+(repository ID), homepage, author (packager), license, and full description.
+
+#### `dnf5_cli_updates` — check for updates
+
+```
+Usage: dnf5_cli_updates [options]
+
+Options:
+  --refresh   Force a repository metadata refresh before checking
+  -h, --help  Show help
+```
+
+Examples:
+
+```bash
+# Check for updates using cached metadata
+./bin/dnf5_cli_updates
+
+# Refresh metadata first, then check
+./bin/dnf5_cli_updates --refresh
+```
+
+### Expected behaviour on non-RPM systems
+
+On a system without an RPM database (e.g. Debian, Ubuntu), the backend will
+log an initialisation error and report itself as invalid.  Discover will
+skip it gracefully and the CLI tools will print a clear error message:
+
+```
+DNF5 backend init failed: Failed to load system repo from root "/": ...
+DNF5 backend not found. Make sure it is built and in the plugin path.
+```
+
+This is expected.  The backend is only functional on RPM-based distributions
+with configured DNF 5 repositories.
+
+## File listing
+
+```
+libdiscover/backends/Dnf5Backend/
+├── CMakeLists.txt              # Build rules, enables -fexceptions
+├── dnf5-backend-categories.xml # Category → RPM-group mapping
+├── Dnf5Backend.cpp             # Plugin entry-point, libdnf5 init & queries
+├── Dnf5Backend.h
+├── Dnf5Resource.cpp            # AbstractResource wrapper around rpm::Package
+├── Dnf5Resource.h
+├── Dnf5SourcesBackend.cpp      # Repository list for the Sources view
+├── Dnf5SourcesBackend.h
+├── Dnf5Transaction.cpp         # Install / remove via Goal + Transaction
+├── Dnf5Transaction.h
+├── README.md                   # This file
+└── tests/
+    ├── CMakeLists.txt           # Builds the three CLI tools below
+    ├── dnf5_cli_info.cpp        # Detailed single-package info
+    ├── dnf5_cli_list.cpp        # List / search packages
+    └── dnf5_cli_updates.cpp     # Check for available updates
+```
+
+## Changes to existing files
+
+| File | Change |
+|------|--------|
+| `CMakeLists.txt` (top-level) | Added `pkg_check_modules(Libdnf5 ...)` and `add_feature_info(Libdnf5 ...)`.  Relaxed minimum Qt/KF6 versions to match the build environment. |
+| `libdiscover/backends/CMakeLists.txt` | Added `option(BUILD_Dnf5Backend ...)` block that conditionally adds the `Dnf5Backend` subdirectory. |
